# Machine-local deploy script (contains my game path)
deploy.bat

# Scratch notes and generated handoffs.
#
# This used to be a blanket `*.md`, which silently made every document in the
# repo invisible to git -- README.md only survived because it was already
# tracked when that rule landed. The project's shipped knowledge lives in docs/,
# so the rule has to be specific about what is genuinely scratch.
HANDOFF*.md
*_Handoff*.md
*_HANDOFF*.md
NOTES.md
scratch/

# Decompiled UnrealScript exported from the game packages with UE Explorer.
# A local research resource only -- this is 2K's copyrighted content and must
# never be committed or published. See docs/modules/gamestate.md for what it is
# good for; regenerate with the CLI documented there.
research/
# Planning: roadmap, session cards, decisions, and feature designs.
#
# Local until the work lands, and that is a deliberate choice about WHEN rather
# than whether. This is a solo project whose planning documents describe features
# well before they exist; publishing a design months ahead of the code invites
# people to build against something that has not been tested in a headset yet,
# and the author would rather announce a feature when it works.
#
# Nothing here is secret and nothing is being withheld from the record. Every
# measurement graduates into docs/ in the commit that uses it, which is where a
# reader would look for it anyway and gives it better provenance than a planning
# note ever had. `docs/` remains the published, permanent knowledge base.
.planning/

# Local Codex <-> Claude collaboration notes. These are transient advisory
# messages and must never become project history.
coordination/

# Submitted log bundles live in research/logs/, which the research/ rule above
# already covers. They carry Windows usernames and machine details and must not
# be committed. The KNOWLEDGE from them is tracked instead, in
# docs/LOG-PLAYBOOK.md -- see the /debuglogs skill.

# Third-party redistributables staged for packaging. Documented in
# dist/runtime/FILES.md; not vendored, because they carry their own licences.
dist/runtime/*.dll
